Les inscriptions sont ouvertes pour le programme Propulsion d'entrepreneur·e·s scientifique de Mila Venture. Il s'agit d'un programme à temps plein de 4 mois à Montréal, conçu spécifiquement pour les fondateurs et fondatrices de la deep tech issus de parcours d'élite en STIM.

Si vous êtes au doctorat, au postdoctorat ou une personne récemment diplômée, que vous portez un projet de startup à haut potentiel et que vous avez la détermination nécessaire pour le bâtir, c'est le programme que vous attendiez!

@hsnorth_: "NEW: Montreal’s world renowned AI institute, Mila, is looking to turn more top Canadian researchers into pioneering founders - and keep them based in Canada. Its investment arm, Mila Ventures, is launching a 4-month 'venture scientist' boot camp this June for researchers with deep expertise in STEM fields - so not something you can find on Google or GenAi - as these people (they’re betting) will be the ones leading the next wave of game-changing startups. Participants will get a $10k stipend and be based out of Mila’s headquarters in Montreal Little Italy. The ambition: produce high-growth startups, potentially even billion-dollar firms. Starting with about 25 for this cohort. The ultimate goal is 100 cutting-edge startups per year."

Check out Lacuna from @tiptreesystems, a machine learning literature navigation tool with a new kind of graph structure. This morning, an ICML workshop paper was accepted at AI4Research, demonstrating Lacuna's usefulness for deep research.

@anirudhg9119: "The team (@nasim_rahaman) is exploring fixing high-level concepts and using 'Alien Space of Science' to generate research (AI for science) proposals to review and provide signal on. Lacuna is an early prototype of this."

Lacuna allows exploring over 700,000 ML research papers across thousands of research directions, authors, and venues.
